{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me understand the full flow:\n\n1. `App.__post_init__` calls `self._setup_state()` — which sets up state manager, socket, etc. if `self._state` is set. Actually `_setup_state` returns early if `self._state` is None.\n\n2. `_enable_state()` — enables state: sets `self._state = State` and calls `_setup_state()`.\n\n3. `_compile_page` calls `compiler.compile_unevaluated_page(...)` which returns `(component, enable_state)`. If `enable_state` is True, it calls `self._enable_state()`.\n\n4. In `compile_unevaluated_page`, if `state is None`, it checks `page.on_load`, `_has_stateful_event_triggers`, and var data with state, setting `enable_state = True` accordingly.\n\n5. `_compile` checks `code_uses_state_contexts(stateful_components_code) and self._state is None` and raises `ReflexRuntimeError`.\n\n6. `_add_optional_endpoints`, `modify_state`, etc. use state.\n\nThe feature request: add an `enable_state: bool = True` field to the `App` dataclass. When set to `False`:\n- Skip state initialization (`_setup_state` etc.)\n- `_enable_state()` should not enable state.\n- `compile_unevaluated_page` should not attempt to auto-enable state (treat components as stateless).\n- `_compile` should not raise the ReflexRuntimeError about state contexts? Actually with state disabled, `code_uses_state_contexts` would still be True if components use state contexts... Hmm. When state is disabled, the compiled output shouldn't include state contexts. Let's think about what needs to change.\n\nWait — the TypeError \"can't access property '$$typeof', Context is undefined\" — this happens in JS when state contexts are referenced in compiled output but `Context` is undefined (because the context file wasn't generated / state isn't enabled). So when state is disabled, the compiled page code should not reference state contexts.\n\nLet me check how components reference state contexts. In `reflex/components/core/state.py` there might be a `StatefulComponent` that references `Context`. Let me look.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"Now let me understand the full flow:\\n\\n1. `App.__post_init__` calls `self._setup_state()` — which sets up state manager, socket, etc. if `self._state` is set. Actually `_setup_state` returns early if `self._state` is None.\\n\\n2. `_enable_state()` — enables state: sets `self._state = State` and calls `_setup_state()`.\\n\\n3. `_compile_page` calls `compiler.compile_unevaluated_page(...)` which returns `(component, enable_state)`. If `enable_state` is True, it calls `self._enable_state()`.\\n\\n4. In `compile_unevaluated_page`, if `state is None`, it checks `page.on_load`, `_has_stateful_event_triggers`, and var data with state, setting `enable_state = True` accordingly.\\n\\n5. `_compile` checks `code_uses_state_contexts(stateful_components_code) and self._state is None` and raises `ReflexRuntimeError`.\\n\\n6. `_add_optional_endpoints`, `modify_state`, etc. use state.\\n\\nThe feature request: add an `enable_state: bool = True` field to the `App` dataclass. When set to `False`:\\n- Skip state initialization (`_setup_state` etc.)\\n- `_enable_state()` should not enable state.\\n- `compile_unevaluated_page` should not attempt to auto-enable state (treat components as stateless).\\n- `_compile` should not raise the ReflexRuntimeError about state contexts? Actually with state disabled, `code_uses_state_contexts` would still be True if components use state contexts... Hmm. When state is disabled, the compiled output shouldn't include state contexts. Let's think about what needs to change.\\n\\nWait — the TypeError \\\"can't access property '$$typeof', Context is undefined\\\" — this happens in JS when state contexts are referenced in compiled output but `Context` is undefined (because the context file wasn't generated / state isn't enabled). So when state is disabled, the compiled page code should not reference state contexts.\\n\\nLet me check how components reference state contexts. In `reflex/components/core/state.py` there might be a `StatefulComponent` that references `Context`. Let me look.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_d6bd6d2fa760479d82210da0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls /testbed/reflex/components/core/ && grep -rn \"Context\" /testbed/reflex/components/core/state.py | head -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"harbor-endpoint","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":555,"output":504,"cacheRead":12416,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":465,"totalTokens":13475,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788494527154,"responseId":"gen-1788494527-7jVHJmwTANjh9Jh8fZnW","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
